WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.860
PROFESSOR 1: I have
the distinct pleasure

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:10.190
of having a Professor Raffaella Sadun
from the Business School of Harvard

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.289
talking to us about
leadership and management.

00:00:12.289 --> 00:00:13.830
RAFFAELLA SADUN: My dad is a surgeon.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.590
My brother is a hospital manager.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:18.800
Every night at home growing
up, I would essentially

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.030
be in the middle of this conversation
between a surgeon resisting

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.970
the managers and the hospital
manager trying to convince

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.940
the surgeon, look, this matters.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.770
And I'll tell you why.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.610
So it's a question that
has always fascinated me.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.970
That said, at a personal
level, the reason

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:39.710
why I'm so intrigued by trying to find
a way for surgeons and hospital managers

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.980
to communicate and work together
in the interest of the patients

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.870
and the whole organization.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.510
At a higher level, I
really think that it's

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:52.370
important to understand ways
in which managers can really

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:55.550
improve firm performance and
through improving firm performance,

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:57.750
have any impact on the
growth of the economy.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:01.240
So I really think that now we
have all the tools established--

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:06.080
this link between the micro level--
what happens in the context of a firm

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.440
and what happens in the
context of a country.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:12.890
It's very important to understand
the internal communication

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:15.230
within these organizations
and really understanding

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:17.610
what is the common objective.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:21.450
This is going to be the
key to prove performance

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.530
for each individual hospital.

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.950
But I feel like this is really the step.

